WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.035
My fellow Americans.

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.870
When I ran for president,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.005
I was told the days

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.440
of bipartisanship are over.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.875
The Democrats, Republicans

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:11.144
can no longer work together.

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:13.279
But I refuse to believe that

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.280
because America

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.248
can never give in

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.150
to that way of thinking.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:17.384
Look,

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:17.884
the only way

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.886
American democracy can function

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:22.489
is through compromise and consensus.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.790
And that's what I worked to do

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.258
as your president,

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.861
you know, to forge bipartisan agreement

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.229
where it's possible

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.897
and where it's needed.

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:33.933
I've signed more than 350 bipartisan laws

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.302
thus far, and with two and a half years,

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.670
including a historic law

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.372
that rebuilding America

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.573
so that we can ranked

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:41.641
number one in the world

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:42.709
in infrastructure

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:43.710
instead of where we ranked

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.879
now number 13 in the world.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:46.913
Another historic law

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.082
rebuilding our manufacturing base

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.984
so that will lead the world once again

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.952
in making semiconductor chips

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.187
so much more

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.388
and so so many more

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.323
and so many more sophisticated ones.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.793
And now a bipartisan budget agreement.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.529
This is vital because

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.164
it's because it's essential

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:04.864
to the progress

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.133
we made over the last few years

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.135
is keeping full faith and credit

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.204
of the United States of America

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.872
and passing a budget to continue

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.541
to grow our economy

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:17.077
and reflects our values as a nation.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:19.646
That's why I'm speaking tonight to report

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:21.347
on the crisis averted

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.015
and what we're doing

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.516
to protect America's future.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.052
Passing this budget agreement

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.554
was critical.

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.756
The stakes could not have been higher

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.357
if we had failed to reach an agreement

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.625
on the budget.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.626
There were extreme

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:34.060
voices

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.462
threatening to take America

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:36.463
for the first time

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:38.665
in our 247 year history

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:41.034
and a default on our national debt.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.302
Nothing,

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.369
nothing would have been

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.004
more irresponsible.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:45.872
Nothing would have been

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.574
more catastrophic.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:48.875
Our economy would have been thrown

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.310
into recession.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.344
Retirement accounts

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:54.013
for millions of Americans would have

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.582
been decimated.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.850
8 million Americans

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.785
would have lost their jobs.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.720
The fault would have been have destroyed

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.522
our nation's credit rating,

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.023
which would have made everything

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:04.991
from mortgages

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:05.959
to car loans

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.527
to funding for the government

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.162
much more expensive

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.163
and would have taken years

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:12.465
to climb out of that hole.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:13.133
And America's

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.701
standing as the most trusted,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.569
reliable financial partner in the world

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:18.505
would have been shattered.

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:21.174
So it was critical to reach an agreement.

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:23.009
And it's very good news

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.611
for the American people.

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.646
No one got everything they wanted,

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.714
but the American people

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.382
got what they needed.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.684
We averted an economic crisis

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.586
and economic collapse.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:34.754
We're cutting spending

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.356
and bringing the deficits down

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:37.957
at the same time.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:40.326
We're protecting important priorities

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.494
from Social Security

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.563
to Medicare to Medicaid

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.197
to veterans,

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:46.299
to our transformational investments

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.834
in infrastructure and clean energy.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.303
I want to commend Senator

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.738
Speaker McCarthy.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.673
You know, he and I,

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.774
we and our teams

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.743
were able to get along things done.

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:57.544
We were straightforward

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:59.179
to fund another completely honest

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:01.681
with a respectful with one another.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.284
Both sides operated in good faith.

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:06.553
Both sides kept their word.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.388
And I also want to commend

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.056
other congressional leaders.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.592
House Minority Leader Jeffries,

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:15.395
Senate Majority Leader Schumer,

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.897
Senate Minority Leader McConnell.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.666
They acted responsibly

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:20.934
and put the good of the country

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.635
ahead of politics.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.103
A final vote in both chambers

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.538
was overwhelming

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.440
far more bipartisan

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.175
anyone thought was possible.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.110
So I want to thank the members

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:31.578
of Congress

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:33.413
who voted to pass this agreement,

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:35.248
which I'm going to sign tomorrow.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:36.849
Become the law.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.551
So here's what the deal does.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.954
First, it cuts spending,

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.455
and over the next ten years,

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:43.690
the deficit will be cut

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:46.025
by more than $1 trillion

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.361
and now be on top of the record,

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:51.631
1.7 trillion, $1.7 trillion.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.466
I already cut the deficit in

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:54.934
my first two years in office.

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:57.503
And it's clear

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:57.870
we're all

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.639
on a much more fiscally responsible

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:00.373
course

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:00.873
than the one

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.375
I inherited when I took office

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.477
four years ago. When I came to office.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.913
The deficit has increased every year

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.881
the previous four years

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.415
and nearly

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.883
$8 trillion

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.051
add to the national debt

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.786
in the last administration.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.922
And now we're turning things around.

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.091
And that's good for America.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:18.558
You know,

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:20.827
my dad used to have an expression.

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:21.427
He said, Joey,

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.528
don't tell me what you value.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:23.496
Show me your budget.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.999
I'll tell you what you value.

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.367
That's at the heart of this debate.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.270
What do we value?

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.138
Protecting seniors.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.840
You may remember during my State

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.541
of the Union address, there were spirit.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.644
There was a spirited exchange between me

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:38.678
and a few Republicans

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.713
spontaneously occurring on the floor

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.482
of the House of Representatives.

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:43.950
I was pointing out that for years

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:44.884
some of them were

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:45.652
putting forward

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:46.286
proposals

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.721
to cut Social Security, Medicare,

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.923
and some of them and I took exception.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.825
And they said very loudly

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.560
that that wasn't true.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.796
So I asked them on the floor that night,

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:59.132
I said, ask them a simple question.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.768
Will you agree not to cut Social Security

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:02.769
and Medicare? Nor

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:05.104
would they agree to protect

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.673
these essential programs,

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:07.440
a lifeline

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.809
for millions of Americans, programs

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:10.543
that these Americans

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:11.044
were paying

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:13.346
into every single paycheck they've earned

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.481
since they started working.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:18.318
And that provides so much peace of mind

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:20.820
with the bright lights and cameras on

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:21.988
those three Republicans

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:24.457
who were protesting They agreed.

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:26.492
They said they wouldn't cut it.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.660
That's how we protected

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.761
Social Security, Medicare

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.296
from the beginning

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:32.732
and from it being cut, period.

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:34.600
Health care was another priority for me,

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.102
a top priority.

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:37.904
I made it clear from the outset

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:39.272
I would not agree

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.407
to any cuts in Medicaid.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.042
Another essential lifeline

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.143
for millions of Americans,

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:46.079
including children in poverty,

00:05:46.079 --> 00:05:46.713
the elderly

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.214
and nursing homes and Americans

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:50.583
living with disabilities.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:51.684
Original House

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.286
Republican proposal would have cut health

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:54.420
care for up

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.622
to 21 million Americans on Medicaid.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.057
I said no,

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:00.893
Medicare is protected

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:01.327
and so

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:04.230
are millions of people most in need.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:04.530
Look,

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.531
I have long believed

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:08.201
that the only one truly sacred obligation

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:09.602
that the government

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:10.570
has is to prepare

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.905
those we send into harm's way

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:13.806
and care for them

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:16.542
and their families when they come home,

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:18.578
when they don't come home.

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:20.646
That's why my last budget

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:22.415
provided VA hospitals

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:23.983
with additional funding

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:26.552
for more doctors, nurses and equipment

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:28.921
to accommodate

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.022
the needs of veterans

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:31.924
and more appointments.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:34.260
The House Republican plan would have met

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:36.262
30 fewer million

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:38.464
VA health care visits for our veterans.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:41.367
We didn't let that happen.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:42.668
In addition,

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:44.070
this bill fully funds

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.172
the Bipartisan Pact Act,

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:47.907
the most significant law in decades

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:48.541
for veterans

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:50.777
exposed a toxic burn pits and for

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:51.544
their families.

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:54.781
Expands access to those veterans

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:55.515
and their families.

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:56.716
To health care

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:59.585
and to disability benefits.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:01.354
Look, we're investing in American

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:04.157
and our people. And in our future,

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:06.959
we've created over 13 million new jobs.

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:10.263
Nearly 800,000 manufacturing jobs.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:11.297
Where is it?

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:12.198
Britain and America

00:07:12.198 --> 00:07:13.332
can't lead the world again

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:14.867
in manufacturing.

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:17.103
Unemployment is at 3.7%.

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:19.605
More Americans are working today

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:22.175
than ever in the history of this country.

00:07:22.175 --> 00:07:23.009
And inflation

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:25.711
has dropped ten straight months in a row

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:28.548
in this debate.

00:07:28.548 --> 00:07:30.483
I refuse to put what was responsible

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:32.018
for all this economic progress

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.820
on the chopping block.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.521
This bipartisan agreement protects

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:36.489
the law

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:37.323
that will help us build

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:40.059
the best infrastructure in the world.

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:42.161
Fully protects the Chips and Science Act,

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:43.563
which is going to bring

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:46.466
key parts of our supply chain to America.

00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:48.601
So don't rely on others

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.403
like semiconductors,

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:51.404
those tiny computer

00:07:51.404 --> 00:07:53.773
chips smaller than the tip of your finger

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:55.208
that affect nearly everything

00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:57.176
we rely on, from cell phones

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:58.878
to building automobiles.

00:07:58.878 --> 00:08:00.513
The most sophisticated weapons system

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:01.547
and so much more.

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:03.983
We protected another law that

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:05.918
I passed and signed last year

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:07.920
that finally beat Big Pharma,

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.056
which I'm trying to do for over 30 years.

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.725
It finally gives Medicare

00:08:12.725 --> 00:08:15.595
the power to negotiate lower drug prices,

00:08:16.262 --> 00:08:17.697
just like the VA has been able

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:19.532
to do for veterans

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:21.234
This law has already dramatically

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:24.036
cut the cost of insulin for seniors

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:27.540
from as much as $400 a month to just $35

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.075
a month for insulin.

00:08:29.075 --> 00:08:31.010
Negotiating lower drug prices

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:33.379
not only saves seniors a lot of money,

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:35.615
it saves the country a lot of money.

00:08:36.082 --> 00:08:38.551
$160 billion.

00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:40.920
It's not having to be paid out

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:41.821
because with

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:43.756
drug prices are more rational.

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:45.091
We pay the highest drug prices

00:08:45.091 --> 00:08:47.126
of any industrial nation in the world,

00:08:47.593 --> 00:08:49.562
and it's just the beginning.

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:50.029
You know,

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:50.897
we also protected

00:08:50.897 --> 00:08:52.131
the most significant breakthrough

00:08:52.131 --> 00:08:53.633
ever, ever

00:08:53.633 --> 00:08:55.668
in dealing with existential threat

00:08:55.668 --> 00:08:57.103
of climate change.

00:08:57.103 --> 00:08:59.672
Today a new wind and solar power

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:02.041
is cheaper than fossil fuel.

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:04.577
Since I've been in office,

00:09:04.577 --> 00:09:06.679
clean energy and advanced manufacturing

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:10.983
have brought in $470 billion

00:09:10.983 --> 00:09:12.652
in private investments.

00:09:12.652 --> 00:09:14.353
It's going to create thousands of jobs,

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:17.423
good paying jobs all across this country.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.191
And help the environment

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:20.927
at the same time,

00:09:21.994 --> 00:09:22.862
Remember, at the beginning

00:09:22.862 --> 00:09:24.063
of this debate,

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:24.764
some of my

00:09:24.764 --> 00:09:26.332
Republican colleagues are determined

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:28.601
to get the clean energy investments.

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:30.836
I said, no, we kept them all

00:09:31.971 --> 00:09:32.371
and there's

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:34.707
and there's so much more to do.

00:09:34.707 --> 00:09:35.341
We're going to do

00:09:35.341 --> 00:09:37.376
even more to reduce the deficit.

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:39.312
We need to control spending.

00:09:39.312 --> 00:09:40.780
If we're going to do that.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.915
But we also have to raise revenue

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:43.282
and go

00:09:43.282 --> 00:09:44.317
